{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/775943-khaibit-ancient-enemies","id":775943,"title":"Khaibit, ancient enemies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-28T06:27:35-08:00","id":775943,"title":"Khaibit, ancient enemies","content":"So the Khaibit are my favorite bloodline and I've just been rereading them and the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">update</a>. After rereading it, it occurred to me that it would be cool if the story update pitted them against the Idigam, which would make all kinds of sense why they have lost purpose, but now the Idigam have returned. Also makes interesting for werewolf crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:21:20-08:00","id":776173,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear that the Strix are intended to be the Khaibit's particular foe.<br /> <br /> That said, it's explicit in their rules in the 2e update of the Bloodline that the Khaibit are capable of fighting other ephemeral entities, so the Idigam are certainly one thing they could go up against. Probably not going to make out too well though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:12:48-08:00","id":776197,"title":"","content":"It's clear that it's there current foe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Khaibit are an ancient line, drawn from Egyptian stock. They come from a Mekhet cult that all but died off centuries ago. Their role was initially to serve Set, and to do his will in forcing back some greater, unknown darkness. While the specifics of their role have been lost to the ages, they now have a different calling; they\u2019re the best known line of defense against the Strix.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>and unless a new book is released that deviates significantly from the stories given in Bloodlines: the Hidden, it sounds like that original enemy may have been something else. If you take Set containing Apep more literally, Apep might have been an Idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:24:07-08:00","id":776204,"title":"","content":"What really happened is up in the air.<br /> <br /> History suggests that Egypt had two groups of magical protectors, one during the night and one during the day. The night guardians were presumably the khaibit and would later devolve into the Followers of Seth, and the day protectors would become the Ascending Ones from Hunter the Vigil. What exactly happened to cause the break-up remains mostly unclear because vampires have meddled with those who recorded history around that point.<br /> <br /> Regardless, in ancient Egypt they defended from 'forces of darkness' that assaulted the nation at night. The strix fit that role perfectly, but you could put any nocturnal creature there you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:36:00-08:00","id":776212,"title":"","content":"The Strix do not really fit this definition though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ancient Egyptians regarded Set as<br /> a dangerous, frightening and evil god...<br /> but it took a fearsome god to protect the world<br /> against yet darker powers. The Sun God could not<br /> rise every morning without Set to battle Apep, the<br /> primordial serpent-demon of darkness. Set kept the<br /> demons in the Netherworld, where they belonged.<br /> The \u201cAsps\u201d aided Set\u2019s work. They walked shadowy<br /> places where other Kindred feared to go, and made darkness their servant. They fought entities from beyond<br /> death and before time began, creatures that would have<br /> destroyed Creation or remade it to suit their own malignant desires. Some Khaibit still maintain their ancient duty, watching gates that must remain closed, and<br /> hunting the servants of the Eldest Powers. Few of them<br /> remain, however. So few to keep the sun rising, a sun<br /> they can never see themselves. </div> </div> </div>Of course a lot of things in WoD fits a lot of those definitions. I'm simply suggesting that Apep might have been an Idigam. Somewhere in here there's also a mention that maybe the thing they were defending against now had more trouble getting here ( spirits gauntlet maybe). I realize I can do whatever I want, just sharing the idea, maybe someone else will like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:44:56-08:00","id":776217,"title":"","content":"The strix fit that pretty well, actually. There's a bit of hyperbole there but the strix could have existed long before vampires, humans and humanity. The mekhet are even explicitly called out as having a non-human progenitor.<br /> <br /> It's very unlikely it was referring to idigam to begin with, as the book came out before Werewolf did, and even then you'd have to wholeheartedly embrace the scarce snippets of information about the idigam, who weren't fleshed out further for years.<br /> <br /> A mage fan might suggest they were talking about the Abyss. But that specific line seems to be part of the vampire obfuscation cleared up, for the most part, in the Mekhet Clanbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:06:17-08:00","id":776327,"title":"","content":"Could it be some Earth-Bound Idigam? Sure. Is it likely? No. An Idigam would have such an easy time turning vampires into bizarre abominations. Fancy Discipline or not.<br /> <br /> Edit: To put it into perspective - With Reaching it could be accomplished <i>from the other side of the Gauntlet</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-28-2015, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T23:20:08-08:00","id":776455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/775943-khaibit-ancient-enemies?p=776327#post776327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could it be some Earth-Bound Idigam? Sure. Is it likely? No. An Idigam would have such an easy time turning vampires into bizarre abominations. Fancy Discipline or not.<br /> <br /> Edit: To put it into perspective - With Reaching it could be accomplished <i>from the other side of the Gauntlet</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would they do that? I'm not an expert on WtF related things, or really spirits. If you're talking about Forge Servant related powers though, those don't appear to work on Vampires. Also give the right power the Khaibit would be aware of any reaching. Though I haven't located any vampiric powers to open a gateway into the shadow realm (they or cotc should totally have something).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T23:22:17-08:00","id":776457,"title":"","content":"Oh trust me. It'd work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T06:51:40-08:00","id":776544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/775943-khaibit-ancient-enemies?p=776457#post776457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh trust me. It'd work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> not big on trust<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idigam may touch a human and, with a Power + Fi-<br /> nesse roll contested by the victim\u2019s Resolve + Composure, tear<br /> his soul free. It may then insert a spirit or soul of the idigam\u2019s<br /> choice into the body. In the case of a spirit, this immediately<br /> creates a Claimed. If the idigam does this with a soul, the<br /> victim suffers the persistent Madness Condition. </div> </div> </div>but vampire's aren't really human anymore... so are you talking about something else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T06:56:35-08:00","id":776547,"title":"","content":"The list of abilities there are not the sole abilities of the idigam.<br /> <br /> But if you want something that transforms vampires into more twisted beings, strix are the standard.<br /> <br /> If you want to use an idigam, use an idigam, you clearly have access to a pdf of the book, it tells you how to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T07:23:47-08:00","id":776560,"title":"","content":"Idigam can twist shit up irregardless of template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:38:07-08:00","id":776905,"title":"","content":"Everybody knows rhe Khaibit began as a servitor cult for one of the Arisen :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T23:49:23-08:00","id":777592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/775943-khaibit-ancient-enemies?p=776560#post776560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idigam can twist shit up irregardless of template.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe that this would be a matter of Storyteller's discretion.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't believe that an Idigam could twist up one of the Arisen for example.<br /> <br /> Also, vampires are explicitly mentioned as &quot;static&quot; creatues, and the changes would be removed under The Cleansing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T02:54:06-08:00","id":777645,"title":"","content":"The same applies to Uratha, yet there you have plenty of examples of the contrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T03:42:27-08:00","id":777662,"title":"","content":"Honestly, what the adversaries of the Khaibit were is completely up for grabs and storyteller fiat, with more than enough room for it to have been a whole plethora of different antagonists across the ages but possibly including:<br /> <br /> - the Strix, or anything else from the Abyss, Inferno, Lower Depths, Underworld, or wherever damn creepy the sodding birds are originally native from..<br /> - some of the adversaries of the Arisen, if not some Arisen themselves.<br /> - Uratha or any other Changing Breeds, because similar ideas and beliefs doesn't have to mean camaraderie, as lots of history and religions show.<br /> - the Idigam, or any other peculiar host of spirits they might feel were overstepping their bounds with humanity or the land, for that matter.<br /> - Ages forgotten Apep-themed ancestors of the Enfant Diabolique.<br /> - some twisted canopic priesthood precursors of the Cheiron Group.<br /> - entities from Second Sight, Immortals, Skinchangers or some other &quot;blue books&quot;.<br /> - vampires from other (current or long extinct) clans or Wicked Dead (ghuls in particular seem to orginate somewhere in the Middle East) just entering Egypt.<br /> <br /> Just for a few examples, not to mention a bunch of other stuff, or maybe all of the above, the degree of threat or interaction depending on region (travelling was not quick or easy, so a degree of regionalization is to be expected) or period of egyptian history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-01-2015, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T07:06:30-08:00","id":777737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/775943-khaibit-ancient-enemies?p=777592#post777592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, vampires are explicitly mentioned as &quot;static&quot; creatues, and the changes would be removed under The Cleansing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The changes fixed by the Cleansing are mostly limited to health and cosmetics, vampires do change on their own, often drastically, and can be possessed or Claimed without any special storyteller's discretion, and it doesn't just fix itself over their daysleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T02:58:17-08:00","id":778214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/775943-khaibit-ancient-enemies?p=777737#post777737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The changes fixed by the Cleansing are mostly limited to health and cosmetics, vampires do change on their own, often drastically, and can be possessed or Claimed without any special storyteller's discretion, and it doesn't just fix itself over their daysleep.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;<b>The Cleansing</b><br /> <i>While Kindred sleep, they return to the time of their <br /> Embrace.</i> Anything that wouldn\u2019t constitute a Health level of <br /> damage heals automatically and returns to its original state. <br /> For this reason, many sires recommend their childer groom <br /> for the Embrace, as part of the ritual of entering the Danse. <br /> If an injury would require Vitae to heal (represented by <br /> Health levels), the vampire will unconsciously heal it during <br /> daysleep. Sometimes, this means the vampire will not have the <br /> Vitae necessary to wake. As she falls to slumber, she may spend <br /> Willpower points to \u201cpreserve\u201d wounds through her rest, to keep <br /> herself from healing them and spending excessive Vitae. This cost <br /> is once per wound, and covers the wound permanently.<br /> Sometimes, Kindred force other marks to remain. For <br /> example, vampires often keep scars, tattoos, and piercings for <br /> spiritual reasons or just to fit in with the flock. Many Kindred <br /> remove long hair, in favor of wigs or cleaner, more modern <br /> styles. The vampire spends Willpower to fight the healing <br /> process while she sleeps. After a day\u2019s rest, any damage heals <br /> as normal, but her body remains changed&quot;<br /> <br /> I would say otherwise.<br /> <br /> Personally i'd say that they can heal every change imposed on them as they would heal a lethal wound, but only while undergoing the Cleansing.<br /> <br /> I cannot argue against Claiming or possession.<br /> <br /> Agree to disagree so we don't mess up the thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T04:18:31-08:00","id":778240,"title":"","content":"I don't really see what the point of bringing the Idigam in is. From a game perspective, I don't see how the Khaibit are going to distinguish between an Idigam and a normal horribly powerful spirit. They both want through to the material world to remake it to their liking. To me it sounds more like the Shadow in general than the Idigam specifically (though it sounds like it could be lots of things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T03:27:43-08:00","id":778892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/775943-khaibit-ancient-enemies?p=778214#post778214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;<b>The Cleansing</b><br /> <i>While Kindred sleep, they return to the time of their<br /> Embrace.</i> Anything that wouldn\u2019t constitute a Health level of<br /> damage heals automatically and returns to its original state.<br /> For this reason, many sires recommend their childer groom<br /> for the Embrace, as part of the ritual of entering the Danse.<br /> If an injury would require Vitae to heal (represented by<br /> Health levels), the vampire will unconsciously heal it during<br /> daysleep. Sometimes, this means the vampire will not have the<br /> Vitae necessary to w